  "unreadable": [
    "wifi-tx-row, middle-row, wifi-rx-row positions 2-7: the 3x8 jumper block prints only 'D7' at the left end and 'D0' at the right end (above the top row and below the bottom row); the six interior columns are unlabeled.",
    "Pad numbers inside the J3/J2 pads are very small; the second J3 pad and the second/third J2 pads were read as 20 and 28/29 from context of the sequence."
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    "Board identity: the silkscreen in the image reads 'Wifi Shield' with a version string ending '...1.3 04/30/2014' (mirrored text, first characters hidden), while the record is Wifi Shield V2.0; the image may show an earlier revision.",
    "J3: one 'GND' label is printed centered between pads 6 and 7 (8 pads, 7 labels); both pads were given GND.",
    "J1 and spi-header: labels are printed in two text columns beside a 2-column header (J1: IO3..VCC / GND..AWAKE, both columns left of the pads; spi-header: MISO,SCK,/RES / VCC,MOSI,GND, both right of the pads). The left label column was mapped to the left pad column; the reverse mapping is possible.",
    "J8/J7/J2: silkscreen prints bare numbers under 'Digital pins' / 'ANALOG'; labels composed as D<n>/A<n> with the bare number kept in functions.",
    "The 3x8 jumper block was split into three 1x8 connectors because each row carries its own printed 1-8 pad numbering; it could alternatively be one rows:3 connector."
  ],
  "notes": "Image shows a Seeed Wifi Shield layout; mirrored silkscreen reads 'Wifi Shield ...1.3 04/30/2014 by Seeed Studio'. A teal 2x3 header labeled ISP (pad numbers ~33-38) has no pin names and was skipped. Reset/WiFi-RST buttons and solder jumpers skipped. The WiFi module itself (diagram marker 2) shows no labeled pins."
